{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260916-78af325943d285fb6e47689c","sequence":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-16T12:06:11.069343Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"e7d357c5-7f7f-4f91-a806-8bd542678a31"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"STORY-260916-1i1gfo","element_type":"story"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260916-d4056d3d0c4c09680fa9dca1","causal_order":2,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"Either the codex seed strips mcp_servers (seeding only trust/model/tui members) or §7.4 and §7.8 state the residual and env status reports the ungoverned seeded entries as §7.6 does for Xcode targets; §7.8 carries the per-adapter asymmetry as a table row; vectors updated"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"The codex seed strips mcp_servers at provisioning (seeding only trust, model and tui members); §7.4 and §7.8 state the rule and the per-adapter MCP-channel asymmetry as a table row; env status lists the native entries that were not inherited; the manager README/CHANGELOG document that a managed codex home runs only the profile MCP set and native ~/.codex/config.toml servers are not inherited; vectors updated"}}]}
{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260916-5d5a7c7595f1b818e36bf5b3","sequence":3,"timestamp":"2026-09-16T18:53:45.639462Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"38aa51b0-1202-4351-b87d-37b76b6553ce"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"STORY-260916-1i1gfo","element_type":"story"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260916-5d3af22e66f94299e7309366","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"description","before":{"kind":"text","text":"Finding E3 (Medium): environments §7.4 seeds codex_cli with the native config.toml copied whole, MCP tables included, and §7.8 layers the profile set over it with -p curator-mcp. A managed codex home therefore runs every native MCP server the operator ever configured, outside the profile lock and outside the §2.2 allowlist, while claude_code runs only the profile set under --strict-mcp-config. The asymmetry is not stated."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Finding E3 (Medium): environments §7.4 seeds codex_cli with the native config.toml copied whole, MCP tables included, and §7.8 layers the profile set over it with -p curator-mcp. A managed codex home therefore runs every native MCP server the operator ever configured, outside the profile lock and outside the §2.2 allowlist, while claude_code runs only the profile set under --strict-mcp-config. The asymmetry is not stated.\n\nImplementation verification (TASK-260916-dv7xv5 rev2, curator main 80483355, launcher main b34e1e27, static): confirmed. Seeds: []string{\"config.toml\"} (envregistry.go:219); gatherSeeds reads the native file whole (managed.go:570-584) and the plan writes the bytes unchanged (:378-388); the other mcp_servers paths are the profile layer renderer (contextmaterialize/mcp.go:231-240) and the read-only home verifier (mcp/mcp.go:253), neither touches the seed. Strip or report belongs in gatherSeeds and the registry seed row."}}]}
